id #uuid "3c3564f2-172b-5ce6-973c-55bb62901f2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-37069" :question/problem "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{12x}{{x}^{2}-4x}.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by factoring the function as much as possible and canceling the common factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12x}{{x}^{2}-4x} & =\\frac{12x}{x(x-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\cancel{x}}{\\cancel{x}(x-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{x-4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\nx-4=0\\,⟹\\,x=4.\n$$\n\nSo the *only* vertical asymptote is at $x=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-37069/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80b8388b-ae0b-5ea6-9efc-fed1a074f463"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-37069"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-68167/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "6e7ce91b-3f31-59b9-8bbc-63367e2a0c00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-68167/selection/d230da838ad595381fb74a8f0cb1688168d4c1bd04af89a235b6dc0914bce51b" :answer/id #uuid "a3de4496-1426-5738-931a-d133a42e61d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-68167/selection/00258c5932d8286b792d219a898959e49995ba251596cc2f3ce2ad266e7bf98f" :answer/id #uuid "60ff823d-86fd-5c48-99dd-36815fa559aa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No vertical asymptotes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-68167/selection/247c7cda7a194bb37a9c36fb92fd681b8fe675772e793d9e3aa74732fd708768" :answer/id #uuid "5156ad7b-3dab-55ee-8611-a179825c8720" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-68167/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "79dee673-ac97-5b5f-b503-49ac24984313" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-68167/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d89f241d-771d-5848-b5f8-7a5814b68cdf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-68167/selection/00258c5932d8286b792d219a898959e49995ba251596cc2f3ce2ad266e7bf98f" :answer-field/choices ["q-68167/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" "q-68167/selection/d230da838ad595381fb74a8f0cb1688168d4c1bd04af89a235b6dc0914bce51b" "q-68167/selection/00258c5932d8286b792d219a898959e49995ba251596cc2f3ce2ad266e7bf98f" "q-68167/selection/247c7cda7a194bb37a9c36fb92fd681b8fe675772e793d9e3aa74732fd708768" "q-68167/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-68167" :question/id #uuid "6ad4d892-a9fd-5ddc-8924-336d5a9c9793" :question/math-academy-id "q-68167" :question/problem "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{3x-2{x}^{2}}{18-12x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's simplify the expression by factoring both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x-2{x}^{2}}{18-12x} & =\\frac{x(3-2x)}{6(3-2x)}=\\frac{x}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the denominator is never zero, we conclude that this function has no vertical asymptotes. A plot of the function is below. Note that it is not defined at $x=\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979852/assets/04c9f0c0e0f8ee16e9eee949d23a816b9ad877ab205d3231bb183a486da97544.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-68167/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "231604dc-fe8f-59be-90fe-37af7a1bb648"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-68167"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-68151/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "79d15cd6-67a4-54e6-b880-1e7db