t/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-4631"] :question/problem "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{(x-1)({x}^{3}+1)}{{x}^{2}-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's simplify the expression by factoring both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-1)({x}^{3}+1)}{{x}^{2}-1} & =\\frac{(x-1)(x+1)({x}^{2}-x+1)}{(x-1)(x+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(x-1)(x+1)}({x}^{2}-x+1)}{\\cancel{(x-1)(x+1)}} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the denominator is never zero, we conclude that this function has no vertical asymptotes. A plot of the function is below. Note that it is not defined at $x=\\pm 1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979852/assets/c76cce145059193c5c5348f2de347ac470f35e8b5392e196ac8b9766382bf2b8.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-107032/selection/00258c5932d8286b792d219a898959e49995ba251596cc2f3ce2ad266e7bf98f" :answer/id #uuid "bc8f2183-c2ce-5e5c-ba85-e1142b6e8cd7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No vertical asymptotes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107032/selection/3156fa3aa006e591d496860456be38662b872375433bbcf5b2f4cb01e08eaa8b" :answer/id #uuid "32d0bb0c-dd8a-56a1-8e0e-294257c95301" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107032/selection/4f6dfb4b0f0751ac323f65f73955b55b1f776b62418ed001d06025d2a8b0851e" :answer/id #uuid "266e6b07-02d9-5aab-98cc-886a115be5b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107032/selection/247c7cda7a194bb37a9c36fb92fd681b8fe675772e793d9e3aa74732fd708768" :answer/id #uuid "f4617fa1-f49e-5ee3-9701-3c921ef021c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107032/selection/264ed6922279f92bdc90c36a26ea47de8f6c6ab903ed9e63c8b8bb51a5a9d4f6" :answer/id #uuid "9f1927f8-e